== Framework ==

Electron
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) Electron contributors
  https://github.com/electron/electron
  Electron embeds Chromium, whose several hundred third-party components
  carry their own notices. Electron generates them all into a single
  `LICENSES.chromium.html`, and Freedom ships that file with every package:
    macOS    inside the bundle, `Freedom.app/Contents/Resources/`
    Linux    beside the `freedom` executable (`/opt/Freedom/` for the .deb,
             the mount root inside the AppImage)
    Windows  beside `Freedom.exe` in the installation directory
  The macOS copy is placed there deliberately, by
  `package.json` `build.mac.extraResources`: on that platform
  electron-builder deletes the copy Electron ships beside the executable,
  and the `.dmg`/`.zip` carry only `Freedom.app`, so without it the file
  would reach no macOS user at all.

